  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Operational and Logistical Assistance to Humanitarian Actors Supporting Flood-Affected Populations across Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The rainy season in Sudan has reached its peak but already displaced more than 96,000 individuals across the country, almost six times more than during the entire year of 2021, according to IOM&apos;s and its Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) monitoring of newly displaced populations across Sudan. Humanitarian actors are, thus, facing significant challenges in reaching the affected communities in addition to shortages of emergency shelter and non-food items. Through this action, IOM aims to address the most urgent gaps in the flood response by providing logistical and operational support to other humanitarian actors with limited or depleted resources, but which are already responding to the floods.</narrative>
  </description>
